Count transmit DMA underflows instead of discarding them

The DAC core reports underflow and overflow in ADI_REG_VDMA_STATUS. The
driver writes the bits back to clear them at preenable and otherwise ignores
them; there is a commented-out dev_warn from 2014 where the check used to be.

So the only way to know whether a transmission was clean was to receive it and
look at the spectrum. docs/modulation-and-throughput.md had to do exactly that
to establish that drops were discrete packets rather than continuous
degradation - a real measurement, made harder than it needed to be.

The bits are sticky and read-to-clear, so they answer "did it happen" rather
than "how often". Sampling them once per submitted block and accumulating
turns them into counts:

    /sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceN/tx_dma_underflow_count
    /sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceN/tx_dma_overflow_count

Writing anything to either zeroes it, because the useful question is almost
always "how many since I started" rather than "since boot".

Measured on the board: a 131072-sample stream fed from a pipe recorded 2
underflows, which is the behaviour the counter exists to make visible - a
short stall at stream start that a spectrum would have had to infer.

